$/={comparison_data:[{factor:"Curriculum",cbse:"Built around NCERT and a structured concept-based syllabus; it is widely aligned with Indian competitive exams such as JEE NEET NEET CUET.[1][3]",cisce:"A broader, more content-rich syllabus with strong language depth and separate treatment of subjects such History/Civics Geography from middle school onward.",ib:"-based, concept-led, interdisciplinary with programmes such as MYP and DP designed around global-minded learning.[4]",flexibility:"Generally more structured with fewer combinations than international curricula.[13]",transferability:"Transfers cleanly between CBSE schools within India; CBSE also has broadest domestic footprint.[8][11]",subject_flexibility:"Generally more structured with fewer combinations than international curricula.[13]",transferability:"Transfers best within CISCE schools but the smaller network can make moves less convenient than CBSE.[8]",subjectflexibility:"Moderate flexibility but still more fixed than IB",transferability_ib:"Best when moving between international schools; recognition is global but local can depend on school level and mapping."}]}
}
